- Design a modern, polished, high-performance interface optimized for extended study sessions.
- Prioritize focus, usability, readability, and fast access to essential study tools.
- Use a clean visual hierarchy with minimal distractions.
- Include a dedicated focus mode with reduced interface clutter and fewer interruptions.
- Use meaningful UI animations and transitions to improve engagement without compromising performance.
- Incorporate:
  - Smooth page transitions.
  - Animated progress indicators.
  - Interactive charts.
  - Subtle feedback animations.
  - Achievement animations.
  - Responsive dashboards.
  - Interactive study calendars.
  - Dynamic roadmaps.
  - Clear test countdowns and status indicators.
- Provide customizable light and dark themes, with a comfortable dark mode for extended study sessions.
- Use typography and spacing that support mathematical formulas, technical content, and long-form notes.
- Ensure the interface works well on desktop, tablet, and mobile devices.
- Optimize navigation so users can move quickly between learning, testing, revision, and analytics.
- Keep the primary dashboard focused on the most important action the user should take next.

## 15. Focus Mode and Productivity Tools

- Provide a dedicated study environment that minimizes distractions.
- Include a configurable Pomodoro timer and custom study intervals.
- Allow users to schedule focused sessions for individual subjects or topics.
- Track focused study time separately from passive video playback.
- Include short break reminders and optional longer breaks.
- Provide a distraction-free reading mode for notes and formulas.
- Offer a study session checklist with a defined objective and completion criteria.
- Allow users to set daily study commitments and review their completion at the end of the day.
- Provide a quick-capture feature for recording doubts, reminders, and concepts to revisit later.
- Prevent unnecessary animations, notifications, and interface changes during active examination or focus sessions.

## 16. PYQ and Question Bank Management

- Build a structured question bank organized by:
  - GATE paper.
  - Subject.
  - Topic.
  - Subtopic.
  - Examination year.
  - Question type.
  - Difficulty level.
  - Marks.
- Store verified PYQs separately from model and AI-generated questions.
- Allow users to filter questions according to their learning needs.
- Track attempted, correct, incorrect, skipped, and bookmarked questions.
- Create a dedicated error notebook containing previously incorrect questions.
- Allow users to revisit questions they found difficult or answered incorrectly multiple times.
- Support custom question collections and revision sets.
- Link questions to relevant concepts, videos, notes, and explanations.
- Track PYQ completion and accuracy by topic to identify areas that need more attention.

## 17. Revision and Mistake Management System

- Create a dedicated revision module that automatically identifies content requiring review.
- Generate revision tasks from:
  - Incorrect test answers.
  - Repeated conceptual mistakes.
  - Forgotten formulas.
  - Low-confidence answers.
  - Difficult PYQs.
  - Incomplete notes.
  - Topics that have not been revised recently.
- Use spaced repetition to schedule revision at appropriate intervals.
- Provide quick revision cards, formula sheets, flashcards, and short quizzes.
- Allow users to mark a concept as understood, partially understood, or not understood.
- Reassess difficult topics after revision to determine whether mastery has improved.
- Automatically remove or reduce revision priority when the user demonstrates consistent understanding.
- Maintain a searchable mistake log with the question, the user's answer, the correct answer, the reason for the mistake, and the corrective concept.

## 18. Supabase Database and User Data Management

- Use Supabase as the backend platform for secure data storage, authentication, and synchronization.
- Implement user authentication and secure account management.
- Store user-specific information, including:
  - Profile and GATE preparation preferences.
  - Target score and examination details.
  - Study schedules and roadmaps.
  - Video history and bookmarks.
  - Notes and PDF export references.
  - Test attempts and answers.
  - Question bank metadata.
  - Performance analytics.
  - Revision schedules.
  - Achievements and rewards.
  - Notifications and preferences.
- Design a structured relational database with suitable tables and relationships.
- Use Row Level Security (RLS) to ensure that users can access only the data they are authorized to access.
- Implement real-time synchronization where useful, such as updating progress and study plans across devices.
- Use Supabase Storage for suitable user-generated files and exported documents where appropriate.
- Implement backups, sensible data retention policies, and secure handling of personal information.
- Store API credentials and privileged keys securely on the server rather than exposing them in client-side code.

## 19. AI Integration and Backend Architecture

- Integrate AI services for summarization, question answering, note creation, question generation, and performance-based recommendations.
- Create a modular backend architecture that allows AI providers or models to be changed when needed.
- Use server-side functions or secure backend endpoints for AI requests that require private API credentials.
- Track token usage, request limits, and processing costs.
- Cache reusable outputs, such as video summaries and generated notes, when appropriate.
- Use available transcripts or captions as source material for video-based AI features.
- Handle unavailable transcripts, inaccessible videos, unsupported formats, and AI processing failures gracefully.
- Validate AI-generated questions and solutions before using them for scored tests whenever possible.
- Store AI-generated content with appropriate source references and timestamps.
- Avoid presenting AI-generated scores, predictions, or recommendations as guaranteed outcomes.

## 20. Security, Reliability, and Performance

- Implement secure authentication, session management, and authorization.
- Protect user data and API credentials.
- Apply database access policies and validate user input on the server.
- Optimize video loading, database queries, AI requests, and dashboard rendering.
- Use lazy loading and caching where appropriate.
- Ensure that active tests are resilient to accidental refreshes or temporary network interruptions.
- Autosave test answers and notes at suitable intervals.
- Provide recovery mechanisms for interrupted sessions.
- Handle network failures, API errors, and unavailable external services with clear feedback.
- Ensure accessible navigation, keyboard support, and readable contrast.
- Make the application responsive and reliable across supported browsers and devices.

