- Syllabus Coverage Tracker: Map every topic to the official syllabus and track its completion status.
- Prerequisite Dependency Map: Identify foundational topics that must be learned before advanced concepts.
- Formula Vault: Maintain a searchable collection of important formulas, derivations, conditions, and shortcuts.
- AI Doubt Notebook: Automatically organize questions and explanations into subject-wise collections.
- Exam Readiness Score: Estimate preparation readiness from syllabus coverage, mastery, revision status, and mock test performance.
- Weakness Heatmap: Visually identify topics with low accuracy, poor retention, or repeated mistakes.
- Mock Test Review Assistant: Analyze incorrect and time-consuming questions and recommend targeted practice.
- Time Management Analytics: Identify questions that consume too much time and suggest areas for improvement.
- Revision Countdown: Prioritize topics as the examination approaches.
- Weekly Strategy Review: Recommend changes to study hours and subject priorities based on recent results.
- Resource Organizer: Allow users to save useful external resources and connect them to relevant topics.
- Study Session Journal: Record daily accomplishments, difficulties, and next steps.
- Offline Revision Support: Make selected notes, formulas, and other suitable study materials available offline.
- Personal Best Tracking: Highlight improvements in accuracy, speed, consistency, and topic mastery.
- Final Revision Mode: Provide a focused interface for formula revision, important PYQs, error notebooks, and full-length mock examinations.

## 22. Integration Between All Modules

- Ensure that every module communicates with the central study planner and learner-performance system.
- When a user finishes a video, the application should recommend the next appropriate activity, such as reviewing notes or attempting a short test.
- When a user performs poorly in a test, the system should identify the relevant weak topics and schedule additional learning and revision.
- When a user improves in a weak topic, the planner should update its mastery estimate and adjust future revision priorities.
- When a mock examination reveals poor time management or weak subject areas, the system should incorporate these findings into the preparation roadmap.
- When a user misses a scheduled task, the system should recommend a realistic rescheduling strategy.
- When the user completes a milestone, the reward system should recognize the achievement and update progress analytics.
- When the remaining preparation time decreases, the planner should reassess priorities and balance syllabus coverage, revision, and mock tests.
- Every significant learning activity should contribute to a unified understanding of the user's preparation status.

The core principle is that the application should not operate as a collection of independent tools. It should function as a single adaptive learning ecosystem in which every video, note, question, test, revision session, and performance result helps determine what the student should do next.

